      "created_at": "2025-10-12T13:19:48.409Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"SimonD\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"155291\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/e274bd/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> SimonD:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In a previous attempt to switch to an open-source solution, we found it difficult to find an accountant who could use the system and collaborate on its configuration.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You’ll likely face the same difficulties here.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"SimonD\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"155291\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/e274bd/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> SimonD:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Is there any list of Belgian accountants who know ERPNext that I could contact?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not that I know of – ERPNext is still quite niche in Europe.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"SimonD\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"155291\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/e274bd/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> SimonD:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also, I’ve tried the Docker installation locally, but the chart of accounts is generic. How can I import a Belgian chart of accounts or an belgian localisation?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><a href=\"https://docs.frappe.io/erpnext/user/manual/en/chart-of-accounts-importer\" class=\"onebox\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://docs.frappe.io/erpnext/user/manual/en/chart-of-accounts-importer</a></p>",
